    ^{:go/apos {0 [1669 2] 1 [1669 65]} :go/pos {:colon [1669 26]}} ["meth:builtins.dict.pop" "D.pop(k[,d]) -> v, remove specified key and return the corresponding value.\n\nIf the key is not found, return the default if given; otherwise,\nraise a KeyError."]
    ^{:go/apos {0 [1670 2] 1 [1670 65]} :go/pos {:colon [1670 30]}} ["meth:builtins.dict.popitem" "Remove and return a (key, value) pair as a 2-tuple.\n\nPairs are returned in LIFO (last-in, first-out) order.\nRaises KeyError if the dict is empty."]
    ^{:go/apos {0 [1671 2] 1 [1671 65]} :go/pos {:colon [1671 33]}} ["meth:builtins.dict.setdefault" "Insert key with a value of default if key is not in the dictionary.\n\nReturn the value for key if key is in the dictionary, else default."]
    ^{:go/apos {0 [1672 2] 1 [1672 65]} :go/pos {:colon [1672 29]}} ["meth:builtins.dict.update" "D.update([E, ]**F) -> None.  Update D from mapping/iterable E and F.\nIf E is present and has a .keys() method, then does:  for k in E.keys(): D[k] = E[k]\nIf E is present and lacks a .keys() method, then does:  for k, v in E: D[k] = v\nIn either case, this is followed by: for k in F:  D[k] = F[k]"]
    ^{:go/apos {0 [1673 2] 1 [1673 65]} :go/pos {:colon [1673 29]}} ["meth:builtins.dict.values" "Return an object providing a view on the dict's values."]
